WEBVTT

00:12.260 --> 00:13.590
Are you gonna do this all day?

00:13.880 --> 00:17.560
I really thought I was gonna die, you know!

00:18.930 --> 00:21.350
It started blowing hot air at me all of a sudden.

00:22.520 --> 00:23.940
<i>It's broken...</i>

00:25.940 --> 00:30.530
It was so hot I couldn't sleep all night...

00:30.820 --> 00:31.780
Well don't go compensating for it now.

00:32.150 --> 00:36.530
Yeah, we have a song to polish before the festival.

00:37.200 --> 00:38.530
What do you mean?

00:39.200 --> 00:41.700
I think it's great.

00:42.160 --> 00:43.040
You mean it?

00:43.660 --> 00:45.830
What do you dislike about it?

00:46.420 --> 00:48.540
Umm, how do I put it...

00:48.710 --> 00:51.300
Sounds a bit too mainstream, I guess.

00:54.380 --> 00:56.140
Tomo-chan, what do you think?

01:04.020 --> 01:08.020
<i>That's it, I've had it with your nitpicking. I'm out.</i>

01:08.190 --> 01:09.690
<i>Same here..</i>

01:14.150 --> 01:16.160
It's fine, isn't it?

02:49.570 --> 02:55.080
A CRESCENT MOON CAME OUT

02:50.040 --> 02:51.830
Why didn’t you say anything?

02:52.500 --> 02:57.210
You told me before something was bothering you about that new song.

02:59.180 --> 03:00.050
No reason.

03:00.930 --> 03:02.350
I thought it was fine.

03:03.600 --> 03:05.930
I see. That's good then.

03:09.810 --> 03:12.230
Still not eating, huh.

03:13.150 --> 03:14.820
You're gonna die at this rate.

03:16.610 --> 03:17.650
Who could that be?

03:18.150 --> 03:19.200
The neighborhood notice?

03:18.150 --> 03:21.950
 TL Note: In Japan, sometimes neighborhoods have a bulletin/notice that circulates between residents, usually through the mailbox.

03:19.570 --> 03:21.950
Ah right, our mailbox is damaged. Could you get that?

03:22.700 --> 03:23.200
Yes?

03:23.370 --> 03:25.530
- Good evening, it's Nina!
- Sorry, we're not interested.

03:25.700 --> 03:27.540
Wait, I haven't even said anything yet!

03:27.700 --> 03:28.450
The hell do you want?

03:28.830 --> 03:29.960
Aah, it's so cool here...

03:30.120 --> 03:32.790
Stop sucking in our cold air!

03:33.130 --> 03:34.710
Eh, it's not like you'll run out.

03:34.880 --> 03:36.800
Keep your voice down you public nuisance!

03:36.960 --> 03:38.760
You’re way louder than me!

03:38.920 --> 03:40.050
Stop ringing it!

03:41.630 --> 03:42.970
I'm in heaven.

03:43.260 --> 03:45.050
Cool off and leave, will ya?

03:45.220 --> 03:47.390
Come on, don't be so cruel...

03:47.720 --> 03:50.890
The AC guy said he'll only come next week.

03:51.060 --> 03:52.480
And how is that my problem?

03:52.850 --> 03:55.690
Does Momoka-san have one?

03:55.860 --> 03:58.570
She does, but she works at night.

04:00.110 --> 04:02.280
By the way, I've been thinking...

04:03.610 --> 04:05.700
isn't yours a bit too weak?

04:04.910 --> 04:06.290
DON'T TOUCH

04:10.540 --> 04:12.250
See, now <i>this</i> feels good.

04:12.540 --> 04:15.040
Much better than your old piece of junk.

04:15.210 --> 04:16.250
It wasn't a piece of junk!

04:16.710 --> 04:19.170
You can't even turn it up, what else do you call that?

04:19.340 --> 04:21.510
It literally said "DO NOT TOUCH".

04:22.010 --> 04:23.130
So as you can see,

04:23.380 --> 04:26.600
both our ACs are out of commission at the moment.

04:27.430 --> 04:31.230
So if you don’t mind, we’d be grateful
if you'd let us cool off for a bit.

04:31.560 --> 04:34.650
Just for a tiny little hour, please!

04:35.020 --> 04:37.150
It’s all this thing's fault, just for the record.

04:38.860 --> 04:41.400
Okay, fine. But just one ho-

04:41.410 --> 04:43.200
OOOOOOOOOUUUUURR?!

04:43.320 --> 04:44.990
He's Tomo-chan's pet.

04:45.360 --> 04:47.200
Apparently he really can't stand the heat.

04:48.990 --> 04:51.370
Don’t just let him out like that!

04:53.540 --> 04:54.420
<i>Powerful.</i>

04:54.710 --> 04:56.080
You’re annoying.

04:56.540 --> 04:58.130
This is one impressive apartment.

04:58.630 --> 04:59.750
Yeah, it's real nice.

05:01.800 --> 05:03.090
It's from Momoka-san.

05:03.760 --> 05:06.430
She said she'll stop by since she works around here.

05:06.890 --> 05:08.510
Got it.

05:06.890 --> 05:08.510
Momoka-san, the other three
barged in here since their ACs broke. Want to come too?

05:06.890 --> 05:08.510
I work close to the Shinagawa
Prince Hotel, I'll be done in 30 minutes and head over there.

05:06.890 --> 05:07.600
Really?

05:07.850 --> 05:11.180
Might as well eat here together then, shall we?

05:08.680 --> 05:10.180
SOUNDS GOOD.

05:12.060 --> 05:14.190
And when did I agree to that?

05:14.810 --> 05:16.810
I remember you saying something about one hour.

05:17.150 --> 05:18.520
Here, just take the- oh.

05:20.440 --> 05:21.940
Oops, guess the last train's gone already.

05:22.230 --> 05:23.110
Seems so.

05:24.780 --> 05:27.450
This was your plan all along, wasn't it?

05:27.870 --> 05:30.200
Now, now, I even brought us some cards to pass the time.

05:30.370 --> 05:31.410
Someone's well-prepared.

05:33.450 --> 05:38.290
We never really had the chance to do something like this if you think about it.

05:38.710 --> 05:41.050
Alright, there's four of us, so-

05:41.210 --> 05:42.250
Count me out.

05:43.460 --> 05:45.130
I’ll be borrowing the bedroom.

05:45.590 --> 05:48.140
I got <i>Ametaro's Rail</i> too if you want. Wanna do the 100-year challenge?

05:45.590 --> 05:48.140
 Reference to the <i>Momotaro Dentetsu: Showa, Heisei, Reiwa mo Teiban!</i> Nintendo Switch game. The 100-year challenge is a very long game mode.

05:48.550 --> 05:50.140
Are you planning to stay here all night?

05:50.810 --> 05:52.390
Did I do something wrong?

05:52.560 --> 05:53.970
I can think of a few things.

05:54.310 --> 05:57.140
Don’t worry, it wasn't your fault.

05:57.690 --> 05:59.020
Are you sure?

05:59.400 --> 06:01.110
I’ll go talk to her.

06:12.450 --> 06:13.740
Heading to bed already?

06:14.120 --> 06:14.950
Not really.

06:15.370 --> 06:18.290
You don't need me for your game night, do you?

06:18.960 --> 06:20.750
I want to be alone.

06:22.960 --> 06:24.010
As you wish.

06:25.460 --> 06:27.550
If you have complaints, I'm all ears.

06:27.930 --> 06:30.970
Complaints? What made you think that?

06:37.980 --> 06:38.560
<i>The loser pays for the food!
Rupa: 20, Nina: 2, Subaru: 10</i>

06:39.980 --> 06:41.060
I lost.

06:41.440 --> 06:43.400
What is even going on here?

06:43.770 --> 06:45.570
Nina, that's what.

06:45.780 --> 06:48.860
If you want to blame someone, blame my AC!

06:49.030 --> 06:50.700
You should have at least tried to suck it up for a bit.

06:51.070 --> 06:51.950
I did!

06:52.280 --> 06:54.290
I killed some time in a convenience store,

06:56.370 --> 06:58.710
I even sat on a bench doing nothing for an hour.

07:00.830 --> 07:04.960
But being outside is super boring when you're broke!

07:05.380 --> 07:06.090
Where’s Tomo?

07:06.260 --> 07:07.420
She went to sleep.

07:08.170 --> 07:10.130
Did she say anything about the song?

07:10.760 --> 07:11.840
Not really.

07:12.260 --> 07:13.100
I see.

07:13.430 --> 07:15.680
She looked like she had something to say back then.

07:16.220 --> 07:17.350
Where are you going?

07:17.520 --> 07:18.560
To the fridge.

07:18.850 --> 07:20.600
It'll be a waste if it gets warm.

07:20.810 --> 07:23.730
And what do you think will happen if my grandmother sees it?

07:23.980 --> 07:27.190
It's fine, it's not like there will be any beer left in them by morni-

07:28.150 --> 07:28.900
A snake?

07:29.200 --> 07:30.610
Tomo-chan's pet.

07:30.860 --> 07:33.740
Don't worry, he's calm and not venomous at a-

07:34.080 --> 07:34.990
SNAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKE!

07:35.950 --> 07:38.620
Phew, saved it!

07:43.000 --> 07:43.750
Momoka-san.

07:43.960 --> 07:45.000
Momoka-san!

07:45.170 --> 07:47.000
Come on, get out of there.

07:47.170 --> 07:49.380
Get rid of it! Hurry!

07:49.550 --> 07:51.880
So she's afraid of snakes, huh...

07:52.050 --> 07:53.390
How traditional.

07:53.590 --> 07:56.600
It's a freaking snake! Are you all just completely fine with this?!

07:57.680 --> 07:58.890
Yup.

07:58.980 --> 08:00.090
This is nuts!

08:00.480 --> 08:03.440
In what world can four out of four girls be okay with snakes?!

08:03.600 --> 08:04.900
You'll get used to it.

08:05.360 --> 08:07.400
There’s a snake right behind you, you know.

08:09.900 --> 08:10.850
IT'S JUST A HAIRDRYER

08:11.820 --> 08:12.560
She opened the-

08:12.620 --> 08:13.260
door?!

08:15.830 --> 08:16.510
Nice beer!

08:16.530 --> 08:17.910
Hey, wait, wait!

08:18.290 --> 08:20.910
- Momoka-san!
- Just get rid of it!

08:21.370 --> 08:24.670
Hey, if you break anything I'm the one who's gonna get it!

08:25.000 --> 08:29.510
We put it in Tomo-chan's room for now.

08:29.880 --> 08:31.590
Just come out!

08:31.760 --> 08:33.430
You’re going to break the door...

08:33.880 --> 08:35.550
I. Said. No.

08:35.720 --> 08:38.140
You’re too old for tantrums!

08:38.310 --> 08:40.430
- You're seriously going to-
- Nina, heads up!

08:43.140 --> 08:44.100
How do you like <i>that</i>!

08:44.810 --> 08:45.650
You gotta be kidding me.

08:46.560 --> 08:48.940
All of you, out, NOW!

08:51.150 --> 08:53.280
Vexing, aren't they. Just like you.

08:54.570 --> 08:56.030
Never come again.

08:58.620 --> 09:01.120
- I’m hot...
- And whose fault is that?!

09:01.290 --> 09:02.710
You get along so well.

09:02.960 --> 09:04.040
No we don't!

09:04.580 --> 09:06.210
Well, I’m off to work.

09:06.670 --> 09:08.170
Good luck.

09:08.340 --> 09:10.210
Get rid of the snake, will ya?

09:11.840 --> 09:13.380
Speaking of which, where did it go?

09:13.550 --> 09:16.760
Subaru-san said she's willing to keep it for a while.

09:17.390 --> 09:18.720
I wish I was a snake.

09:19.560 --> 09:21.220
Alright, time to scatter.

09:21.810 --> 09:23.350
Rupa, let's go.

09:23.560 --> 09:26.100
We should check on the apartment.

09:27.270 --> 09:28.520
You’re gonna ditch me?

09:28.690 --> 09:32.990
And why would we want to see your face outside of rehearsals?

09:33.690 --> 09:37.030
Momoka-san said hanging out together is good for the band, you know.

09:38.490 --> 09:41.790
If you have time, want to watch me practice?

09:43.040 --> 09:45.670
I'll go get my guitar!

09:49.210 --> 09:50.750
An acoustic guitar?

09:51.210 --> 09:51.710
Yeah.

09:52.510 --> 09:57.090
Mine-san told me I should constantly practice if I want to get good.

09:57.590 --> 09:59.600
She said it's a good guitar, even though it's old.

10:00.890 --> 10:02.220
The second string's out of tune.

10:02.390 --> 10:03.020
Really?

10:03.390 --> 10:04.730
You're amazing.

10:04.890 --> 10:07.940
You’ve been playing piano since you were little, right?

10:08.230 --> 10:11.520
That has nothing to do with it. Anyone can hear this much.

10:12.440 --> 10:14.780
Anyway, the guitar is amazing isn't it?

10:14.940 --> 10:19.450
I’m actually starting to get callouses on my fingers from practicing so much.

10:21.740 --> 10:22.910
Is it better now?

10:23.370 --> 10:25.290
Still a bit off,

10:25.500 --> 10:28.790
but I guess that's the best you can do.

10:30.330 --> 10:31.540
Alright, here we go.

10:43.720 --> 10:46.810
<i>What do you think? I thought I could try playing for our next concert.</i>

10:47.020 --> 10:48.890
<i>You've really improved a lot.</i>

10:49.310 --> 10:50.060
<i>I'm all for it.</i>

10:50.400 --> 10:53.520
<i>An extra guitar will definitely spice our sound up.</i>

10:53.690 --> 10:54.320
<i>No way.</i>

10:56.110 --> 10:59.160
<i>Playing at a concert at your level? Are you serious?</i>

11:02.950 --> 11:03.870
Tomo-chan.

11:04.410 --> 11:05.080
Tomo-chan!

11:06.500 --> 11:07.330
How was it?

11:09.460 --> 11:10.420
What do you think?

11:10.580 --> 11:12.750
It's not exactly my area of expertise.

11:13.000 --> 11:16.340
Well, guitar isn't mine either.

11:16.710 --> 11:19.340
But you know music theory, right?

11:20.840 --> 11:21.550
I guess...

11:25.720 --> 11:29.190
I guess it's fine, for an amateur at least.

11:29.390 --> 11:30.230
An amateur?

11:30.560 --> 11:32.100
So I can't play on stage?

11:35.400 --> 11:37.150
Do you want to play on stage?

11:38.320 --> 11:42.030
Seeing Diamond Dust's concert really made me think.

11:42.740 --> 11:44.580
I want to get better.

11:45.580 --> 11:47.450
To stop relying on Momoka-san,

11:48.000 --> 11:50.710
and be able to stand proud next to her.

11:52.790 --> 11:54.380
With you all, of course.

11:55.590 --> 11:59.340
So if there's something I need to improve, tell me.

12:01.840 --> 12:02.720
It was alright.

12:03.260 --> 12:05.890
C'mon, tell me!

12:09.020 --> 12:10.810
<i>If you just keep playing pretend like you are now...</i>

12:11.560 --> 12:14.150
...even your entire life won't be enough for you to learn properly!

12:27.490 --> 12:28.490
I see.

12:30.870 --> 12:32.290
<i>Girls Band Cry.</i>

12:35.080 --> 12:37.380
<i>How many times do I have to tell you? Take it seriou-</i>

12:39.260 --> 12:41.380
<i>Don't judge us by your own standards.</i>

12:42.050 --> 12:46.430
<i>Not all of us won piano awards as kids.</i>

12:47.140 --> 12:48.140
<i>I’m done with this.</i>

12:48.890 --> 12:50.980
<i>- Wait-
- You just shut up.</i>

12:57.770 --> 12:58.690
<i>You know,</i>

12:59.530 --> 13:01.940
<i>We were talking yesterday, and...</i>

13:09.870 --> 13:12.370
It's gotten a bit cooler now, hasn't it?

13:13.870 --> 13:14.790
You think?

13:15.290 --> 13:18.000
It doesn’t hurt to go without the AC for a bit sometimes.

13:18.790 --> 13:21.920
You can feel the gradual change in temperature on your skin.

13:25.380 --> 13:27.470
Still hot in here

13:25.380 --> 13:27.470
Thank you for today

13:32.020 --> 13:34.480
I think Nina was happy, you know.

13:37.100 --> 13:38.690
No way she was.

13:41.730 --> 13:43.860
You got some nerve showing your mug here again.

13:45.110 --> 13:47.740
<i>I, uh, wanted your advice on something...</i>

13:49.160 --> 13:51.370
Wait, wait, I promise I didn’t come for the AC.

13:51.790 --> 13:52.620
<i>Really?</i>

13:54.210 --> 13:57.460
<i>I seriously need advice. Band-related advice.</i>

13:59.540 --> 14:02.380
<i>I’ll definitely pay you back (in 36 installments please). Iseri Nina.</i>

14:07.050 --> 14:07.720
How is it?

14:08.260 --> 14:09.890
What did Tomo say?

14:10.970 --> 14:13.350
That I might as well be playing pretend.

14:13.520 --> 14:16.140
And that I'll never get anywhere like this.

14:17.270 --> 14:18.600
Dang, she sure didn't sugarcoat it.

14:18.770 --> 14:21.400
I guess that's just how she is.

14:24.070 --> 14:25.400
Did it demotivate you?

14:26.700 --> 14:27.410
Why would it?

14:27.820 --> 14:30.410
Well, if that's your reaction, you'll be fine.

14:30.990 --> 14:33.660
So? What do you think?

14:34.330 --> 14:36.410
I guess I kind of agree with Tomo.

14:37.000 --> 14:37.870
I see.

14:38.040 --> 14:41.420
I practiced a lot, so I thought I'm ready for the stage at this point...

14:41.880 --> 14:45.210
You know, even a year or two might not be enough.

14:45.800 --> 14:49.800
Especially if you're trying to go pro.

14:50.430 --> 14:53.220
But you're managing somehow, aren't you?

14:53.600 --> 14:54.600
I'm not so sure about that.

14:55.140 --> 14:59.270
Tomo would probably have a ton of things to say about my playing.

14:59.440 --> 15:01.980
But she never did, right?

15:02.270 --> 15:05.230
Well, that's because I never went out of my way to ask her to like you did.

15:07.240 --> 15:09.410
She’s a bit of a coward in that sense.

15:10.240 --> 15:14.660
She prefers to keep her distance out of fear of being disliked.

15:15.120 --> 15:17.200
And she'll never approach you herself.

15:18.120 --> 15:20.370
On the other hand, if you approach her...

15:23.130 --> 15:24.590
She's a bit like me.

15:25.380 --> 15:28.010
Yep, you were like that at first too.

15:34.850 --> 15:35.810
Sorry for the trouble.

15:35.970 --> 15:38.560
I put him in a terrarium in the back.

15:39.810 --> 15:41.770
He hasn’t eaten anything though, is that okay?

15:42.400 --> 15:43.020
I guess.

15:45.940 --> 15:46.780
Oh, Tomo-chan.

15:48.240 --> 15:49.280
You're still at it, huh.

15:49.700 --> 15:50.240
Yeah.

15:50.740 --> 15:52.700
Subaru-chan gave me some feedback.

15:54.450 --> 15:55.410
Ouch.

15:58.160 --> 15:59.330
It's fine.

16:00.670 --> 16:03.290
Just play on stage if you want to.

16:05.290 --> 16:06.550
Why are you lying to me?

16:19.520 --> 16:20.310
Tomo-chan?

16:23.770 --> 16:24.560
It disbanded?

16:26.520 --> 16:29.940
She came to Tokyo and recruited members online

16:30.530 --> 16:31.820
to start a band.

16:32.320 --> 16:36.240
Is that how you two met?

16:36.780 --> 16:40.960
Yes. There was also a guitarist and a drummer.

16:41.620 --> 16:44.000
They both said they wanted to go pro, but...

16:44.540 --> 16:47.460
Well, that's how it goes. Everyone says that at first.

16:47.960 --> 16:48.880
Really?

16:49.550 --> 16:52.050
You know, people who make it love to say

16:52.680 --> 16:54.890
that they didn’t do anything special to succeed.

16:55.970 --> 16:59.270
Except if that were true, success would be within everyone’s reach.

17:00.140 --> 17:00.770
Exactly.

17:01.430 --> 17:04.060
And Tomo-chan is fully aware of that.

17:04.270 --> 17:07.770
That’s why she’s so strict with us.

17:08.650 --> 17:11.990
She thought we were all on the same page,

17:12.400 --> 17:15.910
so she became more and more demanding as time went.

17:16.870 --> 17:18.990
Yeah, I can see that.

17:20.830 --> 17:24.580
But you still stayed with her.

17:25.830 --> 17:29.380
She did say she wanted to go solo at one point.

17:31.340 --> 17:32.550
Her age was a bit of a problem though.

17:35.930 --> 17:36.760
<i>A guarantor?</i>

17:37.300 --> 17:39.390
<i>I don’t want to contact my parents.</i>

17:40.510 --> 17:42.270
<i>I promise I won't be a burden.</i>

17:44.060 --> 17:47.100
That’s how we moved in together

17:47.610 --> 17:49.520
and created our duo Beni-Shoga.

17:50.270 --> 17:52.230
We were lucky to get some offers,

17:53.030 --> 17:57.160
but she ended up wrecking it every time, huh.

17:57.780 --> 17:58.700
As a result,

17:59.120 --> 18:02.790
she became afraid of saying what she really thinks.

18:03.750 --> 18:07.880
Afraid that if she does, it'll ruin things again.

18:11.460 --> 18:13.170
What do you think?

18:15.300 --> 18:16.180
About my playing.

18:16.800 --> 18:19.350
Would it work live?

18:24.140 --> 18:24.930
Are you seriously asking that?

18:30.020 --> 18:30.980
I figured as much.

18:37.530 --> 18:38.530
I'm back.

18:41.330 --> 18:42.580
Aren't you a bit late?

18:44.950 --> 18:45.960
He's eating it.

18:46.370 --> 18:47.040
Look.

18:49.170 --> 18:49.960
He is!

18:51.460 --> 18:53.630
Being cautious and scared is fine,

18:55.460 --> 18:58.680
but standing still won't get us anywhere.

18:59.090 --> 19:00.090
What do you mean?

19:01.600 --> 19:04.890
Come on, let’s take a walk.

19:10.150 --> 19:12.190
Still as hot as ever, huh.

19:13.860 --> 19:16.110
Starting tomorrow, we're back to rehearsals.

19:17.150 --> 19:19.030
Hopefully it won't rain.

19:20.820 --> 19:22.240
I'm not wrong, you know.

19:23.620 --> 19:25.620
I just told her what she’s worth, period.

19:26.830 --> 19:29.080
She's not good enough.

19:31.330 --> 19:34.500
Then why did you suddenly change your mind after that?

19:34.840 --> 19:35.670
Well…

19:36.630 --> 19:39.510
That's what Nina wants, isn't it?

19:39.970 --> 19:42.970
She wants to play together with Momoka.

19:45.470 --> 19:47.640
That's why she came to you in the first place.

19:48.430 --> 19:49.770
She wants to improve.

19:50.190 --> 19:52.770
That's what everyone says.

19:53.060 --> 19:55.520
"I'm serious", "I want to get better", they all say that.

19:55.940 --> 19:59.610
But in the end, they just want the praise that comes with it.

19:59.820 --> 20:02.030
To sing whatever and however they want.

20:11.460 --> 20:12.830
Hear that?

20:21.550 --> 20:22.050
Ouch.

20:25.050 --> 20:26.140
Umm...

20:26.310 --> 20:29.060
Like this, this, and this dangit!

20:29.980 --> 20:31.810
Do what I say you dumb fingers!

20:36.650 --> 20:38.480
Seeing them play as a trio

20:39.110 --> 20:41.450
made me understand something.

20:42.450 --> 20:44.740
They're serious.

20:45.700 --> 20:48.330
Even if they're far from perfect,

20:48.700 --> 20:51.620
they still give it their all on stage.

20:54.420 --> 20:59.420
I think what you've been looking for all along is exactly that.

21:08.970 --> 21:12.100
You suck!

21:22.110 --> 21:24.110
You'll see, I'll get better!

21:31.370 --> 21:32.370
You suck.

21:37.540 --> 21:40.590
I'm definitely enjoying this.

21:47.760 --> 21:48.800
What's wrong?

21:50.010 --> 21:52.770
I dunno, something's still bothering me.

21:53.140 --> 21:54.020
What exactly?

21:56.650 --> 21:57.690
Nothing, forget it.

21:58.440 --> 21:59.730
Let's take a break.

22:00.150 --> 22:00.900
Momoka.

22:02.610 --> 22:06.450
As it is now, I think this song is boring.

22:15.330 --> 22:16.290
I know, right?

22:26.380 --> 22:28.840
Nina Iseri: Rina Momoka Kawaragi: Yuri

22:30.470 --> 22:33.850
Subaru Awa: Mirei Tomo Ebizuka: Natsu

22:34.890 --> 22:38.270
Rupa: Shuri Tomo Ebizuka: Natsu

23:47.170 --> 23:48.840
<i>Next up: "Wandervogel".</i>
